{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"91723ce7-e88b-4dd9-a674-debccb514ec4","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I am installing `effect@latest` in the background and will proceed once the installation completes.\nWaiting for `npm install effect@latest` to finish.\nStill waiting for package installation to complete.\nContinuing to wait for `npm install effect@latest` to finish downloading and linking packages.\nChecking TypeScript compilation.\nWaiting for test suite to finish.\nWaiting for the remaining tests (retrying 500 error and network failure) to complete.\nThe exchange rate CLI has been rewritten using Effect 4 (`4.1.2`).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Installed Effect 4 (`effect@latest`)**:\n   - Upgraded to `effect@4.1.2` directly without `@effect/platform` (as HTTP client functionality is built into `effect/http` in Effect 4).\n\n2. **Modeled Rates API as a Service with a Layer**:\n   - Created `RatesService` extending [`Context.Service`](file:///tmp/h-HfLiik/src/main.ts#L22-L65).\n   - Read the base URL via [`Config.String(\"RATES_URL\")`](file:///tmp/h-HfLiik/src/main.ts#L27).\n   - Configured the HTTP client with `FetchHttpClient.layer`, `HttpClientRequest.prependUrl`, `HttpClientRequest.acceptJson`, and `HttpClient.filterStatusOk`.\n   - Added `HttpClient.retryTransient({ schedule: Schedule.exponential(50), times: 3 })` to retry transient network and 5xx errors with exponential backoff starting at 50 ms.\n\n3. **Schema Validation**:\n   - Modeled the response structure with `Schema.Struct({ base: Schema.String, date: Schema.String, rates: Schema.Record(Schema.String, Schema.Number) })`.\n   - Used `HttpClientResponse.schemaBodyJson(RatesResponse)` to validate the response body, catching schema decoding errors and non-JSON body errors as `InvalidResponseError`.\n\n4. **Output and Exit Codes**:\n   - Exit 0: On success, logs `1 USD = 0.9214 EUR` (with 4 decimal places).\n   - Exit 1: If quote currency is not in rates, prints `unknown currency: XYZ` to `stderr`.\n   - Exit 2: If response body fails schema validation or is not valid JSON, prints `invalid response` to `stderr`.\n   - Exit 3: Any other error (network failure after retries, 4xx/5xx status, missing env variable, CLI arguments error, etc.).\n\n5. **Colleague's Note Review**:\n   - Created [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-HfLiik/ANSWER.md) detailing which parts of the colleague's note applied and which were adapted.\n\n### Verification\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes cleanly.\n- `npm ls effect` confirms `effect@4.1.2` with no `@effect/platform`.\n- All exit codes and retry behaviors were tested and verified against a mock HTTP server.\n","duration_seconds":699.479816,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":458520,"output_tokens":17250,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":3767171,"total_tokens":475770}}}
